            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2289,
              "end_index": 2492,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Criminal Liability:** While misfeasance itself is a civil matter, in serious cases, particularly those involving elements of fraud, theft, or false accounting, directors could face criminal prosecution"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              2
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2499,
              "end_index": 2710,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Professional and Reputational Damage:** A finding of misfeasance can lead to diminished future employability, especially at senior levels, and potentially the loss of professional qualifications or memberships"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              1,
              2,
              3,
              14,
              4,
              9,
              6,
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2768,
              "end_index": 2866,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Misfeasance claims predominantly arise when a company enters **liquidation** or **administration**"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              1,
              3
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2868,
              "end_index": 3021,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The appointed insolvency practitioner (liquidator or administrator) is legally obliged to investigate the director's actions leading up to the insolvency"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              2,
              3,
              14,
              18,
              15,
              9,
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3023,
              "end_index": 3129,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Claims can also be brought by creditors, a contributory to the company's capital, or the Official Receiver"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              1,
              2,
              15,
              9,
              6,
              7,
              8,
              19
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3132,
              "end_index": 3252,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The primary legal basis for misfeasance claims against directors is **Section 212 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (IA 1986)**"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              15,
              9,
              8
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3254,
              "end_index": 3479,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This provision grants the court the power to examine the conduct of directors and compel them to account for misapplied money or property, or to contribute to the company's assets as compensation for the misfeasance or breach"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3481,
              "end_index": 3591,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The **Companies Act 2006** also holds directors personally liable for losses to creditors in misfeasance cases"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              9
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3591,
              "end_index": 3713,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": ", and the duties outlined in **Sections 171 to 177 of the CA 2006** define the standard of conduct expected from directors"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              2,
              16,
              9,
              5,
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3757,
              "end_index": 3858,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Disqualification Period:** If found unfit, a director can be disqualified for **2 to 15 years**"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              1,
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3860,
              "end_index": 4004,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Limitation Period for Misfeasance Claims:** Generally, misfeasance proceedings must be issued within **six years** of the relevant conduct"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              1,
              18,
              19,
              20
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4006,
              "end_index": 4226,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "However, different limitation rules may apply for breaches of trust or fiduciary obligations, and in cases where a director unlawfully transfers property to a company they control, there might be **no limitation period**"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              16
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4228,
              "end_index": 4339,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The six-year period can run from the date of the conduct or from when the company entered an insolvency process"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4341,
              "end_index": 4517,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Disqualification Proceedings Timeline:** Disqualification proceedings must be issued within **three years** of the company being placed into liquidation or administration"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4607,
              "end_index": 4726,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Being unaware or acting as a non-executive or part-time director is generally not a defence against a misfeasance claim"
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              18,
              10,
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4728,
              "end_index": 4832,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Early professional advice is crucial if financial difficulties arise or misfeasance allegations are made"
            }
          }
        ],
